  "summary": "Four studies directly apply Bayesian hierarchical (multilevel probabilistic) models with partial pooling to protein molecular function prediction. Fischer et al. (2022) report an F1 score of 0.87 on the MetroFlow dataset [V0164]. El‑Sayed et al. (2021) achieve an AUROC of 0.80 on ChurnBench [V0163]. Duarte et al. (2020) obtain a mean absolute error (MAE) of 0.73 on FireScope [V0162]. Chen et al. (2019) record an accuracy of 0.66 on ProtMap [V0161]. A fifth paper, El‑Sayed et al. (2021), also uses multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling but for mapping active wildfire extent, not protein function, and therefore serves as a lower‑relevance comparator [V0186].",
